      "claim": "In fantasy and mythological lore a \"true name\" is a magical identifier that represents the essence of a being.",
      "evidence": "Sources such as Ursula K. Le Guin’s Earthsea, Dungeons & Dragons rules, and folklore (e.g., Rumpelstiltskin) describe true names as the metaphysical core of a creature.",
